# Rack map (`ghq_rack_map.js`)

## Role

Single source of truth for **what** the command center can control on `2026 Guitar Rack`. The engine scans Live; the map defines expected devices, parameters, and UI metadata.

## Control entry shape

- **`id`:** stable string used in UI `controlId` and engine bindings (must be unique)
- **`label` / `section`:** UI grouping
- **`kind`:** drives engine behavior (`slider`, `toggle`, `select`, `device_toggle`, …)
- **`deviceKey`:** key into `deviceAliases`
- **`parameter`:** array of acceptable Live parameter names (first match wins)
- **`chainName`:** for amp chain toggles — binds that chain’s `chain_activator` on the `deviceKey` rack
- **`value`:** for `select` (discrete chain index), if used
- **`defaultNormalized`:** optional initial when unbound
- **`detail: true`:** editor-only dense controls
- **`optional: true`:** missing device does not count against `boundCount`

## Device aliases

`deviceAliases[deviceKey]` lists name variants (case-insensitive normalized match). Add aliases when users report scan misses — not arbitrary renames in Live sets.

## Tests (`ghq_rack_map.test.js`)

Run after map edits:

```sh
node ghq_rack_map.test.js
```

Validates: unique `id`, required fields, `deviceKey` exists in `deviceAliases`, `parameter` present for slider/toggle/select kinds.

## Live verification

Automated tests do not call LiveAPI. After map or alias changes, sync to User Library and **Scan** in Live next to the real rack.
